.TH "SOPLOS-WELCOME" "1" "2026-10-21" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-welcome \- Welcome and system setup application for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-welcome
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-welcome
is the welcome and system configuration application for Soplos Linux.
Built with Tauri 2, Rust, and Svelte, it gives one place to update the system,
install drivers and kernels, harden security, pick applications, tune the
desktop and optimize the machine for gaming. It is organized in eight sections:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B Home:
system overview, hardware specifications, display server (X11 or Wayland),
desktop environment and quick action shortcuts.
.IP \[bu]
.B Software:
APT, Flatpak (user, system or both scopes), Snap and Flathub management,
system update and upgrade, and Flatpak runtime cleanup.
.IP \[bu]
.B Drivers:
hardware detection with NVIDIA proprietary drivers, the CUDA toolkit,
AMD ROCm, Intel oneAPI, Broadcom and MediaTek Wi-Fi firmware, and the
VirtualBox and VMware guest and host tools.
.IP \[bu]
.B Kernels:
the Soplos Kernels repository, XanMod and Liquorix kernels, removal of old
unused kernels, and integration with Soplos Kernel Installer.
.IP \[bu]
.B Security:
firewall management with UFW, antivirus scans with ClamAV, rootkit detection
with rkhunter, VPN configuration and system hardening checks.
.IP \[bu]
.B Recommended:
about 100 curated applications across 12 categories, with single or multiple
selection for batch installation and removal, and extended search.
.IP \[bu]
.B Customization:
desktop personalization tools for Xfce, GNOME and KDE Plasma, the wallpaper
manager and font rendering presets.
.IP \[bu]
.B Gaming:
game launchers (Steam, Heroic, Lutris, Bottles), GameMode, low-latency sysctl
tuning, GPU optimizations and the MangoHud overlay.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.P
The window never runs as root. Administrator tasks are run through
.BR pkexec (1)
under the Polkit action declared by the package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.TP
.B \-\-run-privileged-script \fIFILE\fR
Internal Polkit-authenticated task: run the privileged script stored in
.IR FILE .
Used by the application itself through
.BR pkexec (1)
and not meant to be called by hand.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab
Next section.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Previous section.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.welcome.policy
Polkit policy defining the administrator privileges for driver and system operations.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/org.soplos.welcome.desktop
Autostart entry created or removed from the application, to open it at session login.
.TP
.I ~/AppImages/
Where AppImages installed from the Recommended section are stored.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/
Desktop entries created for the applications installed from the Recommended section.
